      "writtenOn": "2026-10-05T11:25:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, it walks fewer.                                                                                                                                                                            \n\nThe walk adds the change\u0027s commit and all accepted commits to one queue and always processes the newest commit first. That way, \"accepted\" marks pass down history before the walk reaches the commits below them. Otherwise a commit that is reachable from an accepted tip could be reported as missing.                                                                                    \n\nBefore, every branch and tag tip was accepted. Tips newer than the change\u0027s commit came out of the queue first, and their history had to be walked back to the change\u0027s date before the walk could finish, even though accepting the parents already gave the correct answer.                                                                                                               \n\nNow the parents are the only accepted commits. Nothing in the queue is newer than the change\u0027s commit, so the walk handles it, reaches its parents and stops.",
      "parentUuid": "421ba3ef_84d6b138",
      "revId": "59f3e1ca5f9164af507f5d753a8f2d82c10c1c06",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    }
